# Deadcode Allowlist (tool metadata – intentionally not end-user docs)

// Patterns (one per line) for unreachable functions intentionally kept.
// Lines starting with // are comments.
// Core CLI root accessor (used indirectly via tests/build tooling)
GetRootCommand # rationale: Root Cobra command accessed indirectly via test harness & binary entrypoints; removing breaks CLI composition tests
// API response helper (204 no body). Covered by TestAutoNoContentAndNotFound in internal/api/response/response_test.go
AutoNoContent204 # rationale: 204 helper only invoked in integration tests; keeps stable API envelope semantics without inline duplication
// Config validation helpers publicly documented in README
ValidateAllConfig # rationale: Publicly documented startup validation API; indirect usage through integration layers not seen by deadcode tool
EnsureConfigDirectories # rationale: Side-effect directory preparation separated from validation; invoked in startup path via DI wiring
// QueryBuilder primitives exercised indirectly (builders used in analytics facade)
NewFOCUSQueryBuilder # rationale: Factory exercised through higher-level analytics facade; retained for external provider extensibility
FOCUSQueryBuilder.Select # rationale: Fluent interface method used via reflection in extended builds; chained usage sometimes elided in static analysis
FOCUSQueryBuilder.From # rationale: See Select; explicit retention ensures stable public chaining surface
FOCUSQueryBuilder.Where # rationale: Conditional query assembly in analytics facade; deadcode tool misses due to build tags
FOCUSQueryBuilder.GroupBy # rationale: Required for aggregate analytics queries; indirect calls via generated builders
FOCUSQueryBuilder.OrderBy # rationale: Sorting added conditionally; retained for stable DSL completeness
FOCUSQueryBuilder.Limit # rationale: Optional pagination path; invoked only in enterprise analytics variants
FOCUSQueryBuilder.Offset # rationale: Paired with Limit; same enterprise-only path
FOCUSQueryBuilder.SelectCostMetrics # rationale: Consolidates metric column selection; reused across multiple builders
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByProvider # rationale: Provider scoping when multi-cloud datasets loaded; triggered conditionally
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByDateRange # rationale: Date range filter injected via options object; analyzer misses Option indirection
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByCostThreshold # rationale: Threshold filter compiled only when flag provided; sporadic test coverage
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByService # rationale: Service dimension filtering; kept for DSL symmetry & roadmap
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByRegion # rationale: Region predicate insertion under regional analytics flag
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByAccount # rationale: Account scoping; enterprise tenancy evolution relies on it
FOCUSQueryBuilder.FilterByTenant # rationale: Multi-tenant feature flag path; presently gated but required for Phase 2 enforcement
FOCUSQueryBuilder.Build # rationale: Terminal builder assembling SQL string; indirect through facade wrappers
BuildTopServicesByCost # rationale: Helper used by generated analytics code in duckdb build; slim build prunes references
BuildCostTrendByTime # rationale: Trend analytics path executed only with focus engine flag
// Multitenant helpers (feature flag future use)
InjectTenantFilter # rationale: Feature-flagged multi-tenant predicate injector; activation pending rollout
EffectiveTenant # rationale: Resolves tenant precedence (header/ctx) for future enforced queries
// Enterprise gating / disabled paths (metrics + errors)
IsDisabled # rationale: Enterprise gating helper used in stubs; ensures consistent disabled error semantics
ObserveDisabled # rationale: Emits unified metrics for disabled enterprise features; invoked in test toggles
// Parity hash (used by parity tool; exposed as CLI pipeline helper)
HashFocusLite // In-memory lite parity hash (unit & mapper parity tests) mirrors computeLiteHash in scripts/tools/parity-check; removing forces DuckDB dependency in tests. # rationale: Maintains cross-tool parity without heavyweight dependencies

// Enhanced production service enterprise stub (community build keeps API surface; methods emit disabled metrics)
EnhancedProductionService # rationale: Enterprise stub preserves public interface; replaced under enterprise build tag

// Enterprise connection manager (enterprise-only pooling/metrics; stub keeps CreateConnectionPool API in community build)
EnterpriseConnectionManager # rationale: Stub ensures API stability; enterprise implementation adds pooling metrics

// TenantContext test-only middleware helper (kept to validate tenant propagation without coupling tests to prod buildTenantMiddleware)
TenantContext # rationale: Test-only middleware helper enabling tenant propagation assertions without exporting prod internals

// RBAC audit mode test hook; toggles atomic flag without process restart (invoked in multiple permission*_test.go)
SetAuditModeForTests # rationale: Atomic RBAC audit flag toggler needed for deterministic permission tests

// Advanced analytics experimental gating: disabled stub (no experimental tag) retains API surface and emits enterprise feature metrics
AdvancedAnalyticsService # rationale: Experimental analytics stub; preserves contract when experimental tag omitted
NewAdvancedAnalyticsService # rationale: Factory returning disabled stub when feature tags absent; referenced in CLI wiring
ErrDisabled # rationale: Canonical sentinel error for disabled enterprise/experimental features used in tests & handlers
